<!--
    Framework manifest for the recovery.

    hwservicemanager only ever reads /system/etc/vintf/manifest.xml and the
    legacy /system/manifest.xml. It does not walk the
    /system/etc/vintf/manifest/ directory, so a fragment there is silently
    ignored and hwservicemanager comes up with an empty framework manifest.

    With nothing declared it refuses to serve its own transports:

      hwservicemanager: getTransport: Cannot find entry
        android.hidl.manager@1.2::IServiceManager/default in either
        framework or device VINTF manifest.

    keystore2 asks for IServiceManager as its very first step and dies with
      Check failed: serviceManager.get() Failed to get ServiceManager
    followed by SIGABRT, on a five second loop. /data therefore never gets
    decrypted and the recovery sits on the OrangeFox logo forever.

    ITokenManager is declared as well because hwservicemanager hosts it from
    the same process and looks it up through the same table.
-->
<manifest version="1.0" type="framework">
    <hal format="hidl">
        <name>android.hidl.manager</name>
        <version>1.2</version>
        <transport>hwbinder</transport>
        <interface>
            <name>IServiceManager</name>
            <instance>default</instance>
        </interface>
    </hal>
    <hal format="hidl">
        <name>android.hidl.token</name>
        <version>1.0</version>
        <transport>hwbinder</transport>
        <interface>
            <name>ITokenManager</name>
            <instance>default</instance>
        </interface>
    </hal>
</manifest>